          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Decide on the family first: a lawn tractor for slopes, towing and versatility, a zero-turn for flat lawns full of obstacles. Then choose a hydrostatic transmission unless your lawn is simple and flat, size the deck to your gates and acreage, and favor a V-twin engine if you have thick grass or plan to tow.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
